Z||000014||doughboySE||03-02-2000||06:49 PM||||you want to annoy someone <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> build the box i did it was cheep cause i used all the wood from the box the sub was in before and that 12 inch rocks im thinking of doing the same next year behid my seat (thats if this weekend goes ok sinking the box in 2 inches)<BR>my wife used to tell me she could hear the boom from 3 blocks away when i had this sub in my VW and im sure its close to the same now. DAMN THE COPS WILL BE AFTER ME THIS YEAR <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||stimpy||03-02-2000||08:50 PM||||Bass Shakers are a product manufactured by Aura. Won best new product of the year when they came out at Las vegas electronics show. Problemis, they are not flashy.  You get 2 6" magnet-looking things that are faced with corkboard that mount flat to the floor of the car. (Carpet must be removed under the seat.) This turns the floor under your seat into a giant woofer basically. Really deep bass is more felt then heard, so these work on the priciple of the sound actually traveling through your skeleton.  Personally, I am more into hitting hard beats and low boom that gets the girlfriend excited then pissing off my neighbors and getting tickets. You really don't hear bass outside of the car with these. Sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000016||spike||03-04-2000||12:22 PM||||I wish I could give you people all the specs to my box but if I did that I would have nothin to look forward to. I will be getting my new Fiero GT soon I hope. I have been waiting for an answer from a scrap yard for about 3 months. They have an 87 GT with light front & rear end damage. Only thing about the car I dont like is the fact that there is no sun roof. My last GT had one and it was great. I plan on installing a 4.3L in this car and doing some body modes. Once I get my Fiero I will build the sub box AGAIN. This time I might put 2 12's. My other box had 10's which did work well but with a little box midification 12's would not be a problem.<BR>I plan on building about 10 boxes and hitting the road this summer to attend some club meetings so keep your eyes open. I have asked what a fare price would be but didnt realy get an answer. It costs about 80-100 CDN. in material & about 5-6HRS. of work. The box is a little tricky to build, all sides are angled and it is a perfect fit. Nothing is needed to keep it in place. Seat loss is about 1-2 inches max. Best of all you dont have to rip your inside apart. With this system the subs are totally visable to all so a good alarm is recommended.<BR>||||reg||1
